nodes.body:
@LucasWilkinson @MatthewBonanni hope you're having a good day ,  I actually went through the entire  PR and the code path for the issue #60174 , The fix looks reasonable to me and the ablation results line up with the issue especially the 64 vs 1648 block size mismatch and the fact that picking a divisor restores the = old behavior.  

A small thing which I discovered was that the current tests cover _largest_dividing_kernel_block itself but there isnt a test that verifies get_kv_cache_spec which actually passes the constrained block through to the final KV cache spec. It might be worth adding a small integration level test for the same since otherwise the helper could theoretically regress at the call site without the existing tests catching it up. 

Other than that it looks good to me. Nice work on building this fix @ZeroKernel798 ! Looking forward to getting this merged (;

